  "question": {
    "text": "A normal is drawn to the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> at the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> where <math><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> If <math><mi>N</mi></math> is the foot of the perpendicular from the origin&nbsp;<math><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;to the normal such that <math><mi>O</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>, then <math><mi>&#952;</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
